   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Stressed pronoun + qui",
     "texto": [
      "With a stressed pronoun **c'est** is used for the singular and **ce sont** for the plural: **C'est moi qui ai décidé** (it was me who decided). **Ce sont eux qui ont gagné** (it was they who won)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Watch out",
     "texto": [
      "With nous and vous one also says **c'est nous qui** or **c'est vous qui**: **C'est nous qui sommes responsables** (it's us who are responsible)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Stressed pronoun",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "With «c'est» / «ce sont» (may include pieces of the language you are studying; copy those as they are)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
